# Only the junk removal folder is ever copied into the image, so everything
# else is excluded from the build context. Without this, Docker uploads the
# whole repo — including blog/ (a full WordPress install, ~4200 files) and the
# 279-file images/ folder — on every build, for no reason.
*
!junk-removal

# Build tooling and docs do not belong in a web root.
junk-removal/_pages
junk-removal/_build.py
junk-removal/images/_make-icons.py
junk-removal/README.md
junk-removal/MIGRATE.md
junk-removal/.github
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
